{
"name":"CO2-Adaptive","powerIndexFilterFactorUp":{
"doc":"\nLow pass filter factor. 1 = no low-pass filter. 2 = filter factor 1 (fast) ... 10 = very slow.\nWhen the built-in ADR function propose a new slower power index, this filter factor is employed in a low pass filter.\nIf the filter value is set to 1 the algorithm will use its proposed new value (if below or at max).\n","uiName":"LoRaWan power filter factor up","unit":"Integer","min":1,"max":50,"default":3,"size":1,"translate":1,"id":160,"type":"input","name":"powerIndexFilterFactorUp"},"powerIndexFilterFactorDown":{
"doc":"\nLow pass filter factor. 1 = no low-pass filter. 2 = filter factor 1 (fast) ... 10 = very slow.\nWhen the built-in ADR function propose a new faster power index, this filter factor is employed in a low pass filter.\nIf the filter value is set to 1 the algorithm will use its proposed new value (if below or at max).\n","uiName":"LoRaWan power filter factor down","unit":"Integer","min":1,"max":50,"default":3,"size":1,"translate":1,"id":161,"type":"input","name":"powerIndexFilterFactorDown"},"maxPowerIndex":{
"doc":"\nMaximum power index to use for LoRaWan traffic, including join. The firmware's table of data rate\nand TX power steps decides how high it goes, and that depends on the region: 16 today, but 13 in\nUS915, where the table stops at DR4. 255, the default, is the top of the table whatever the region,\nso a longer table in a later firmware is used as it is. A value above the top is lowered to it,\nand reads back as the index in use.\n","uiName":"Max Power Index","unit":"LoraWan power index","min":0,"max":255,"default":255,"size":1,"translate":1,"id":162,"type":"input","name":"maxPowerIndex"},"co2_limit_ppm":{
"doc":"\nThe CO2 limit. Above it the sensor is sampled every high_poll_minutes and reports go out every\nhigh_report_interval_minutes. Crossing it either way sends a report.\n\n","uiName":"CO2 Limit","unit":"ppm","default":1000,"min":400,"max":5000,"size":4,"translate":1,"id":184,"type":"input","name":"co2_limit_ppm"},"co2_led_enable":{
"doc":"\n1 makes the LED give one short red blink at each sample while CO2 is above the limit, which is\nevery high_poll_minutes. 0 keeps the LED dark.\n\n","uiName":"CO2 LED","default":0,"min":0,"max":1,"size":1,"translate":1,"id":164,"type":"input","name":"co2_led_enable"},"dark_report_interval_minutes":{
"doc":"\nMinutes between reports while the room is dark and CO2 below the limit, sent whether anything\nchanged or not. 0, here or in lit_report_interval_minutes, turns the measurement off and powers\nthe CO2 sensor down.\n\n","uiName":"Dark Report Interval","unit":"Minutes","default":15,"min":0,"max":1440,"size":4,"translate":1,"id":185,"type":"input","name":"dark_report_interval_minutes"},"lit_report_interval_minutes":{
"doc":"\nMinutes between reports while the lights are on and CO2 below the limit, sent whether anything\nchanged or not. 0, here or in dark_report_interval_minutes, turns the measurement off.\n\n","uiName":"Lit Report Interval","unit":"Minutes","default":15,"min":0,"max":1440,"size":4,"translate":1,"id":186,"type":"input","name":"lit_report_interval_minutes"},"high_report_interval_minutes":{
"doc":"\nMinutes between reports while CO2 is above the limit, whatever the light.\n\n","uiName":"High CO2 Report Interval","unit":"Minutes","default":5,"min":1,"max":60,"size":1,"translate":1,"id":165,"type":"input","name":"high_report_interval_minutes"},"co2_check_minutes":{
"doc":"\nMinutes between checks of whether CO2 has moved, while CO2 is below the limit. When the latest\nsample is co2_step_ppm or more from co2_current as last reported, a report goes out without\nwaiting for the interval.\n\n","uiName":"CO2 Check Interval","unit":"Minutes","default":5,"min":1,"max":60,"size":1,"translate":1,"id":166,"type":"input","name":"co2_check_minutes"},"high_co2_check_minutes":{
"doc":"\nMinutes between checks of whether CO2 has moved, as co2_check_minutes, while CO2 is above the\nlimit.\n\n","uiName":"High CO2 Check Interval","unit":"Minutes","default":5,"min":1,"max":60,"size":1,"translate":1,"id":167,"type":"input","name":"high_co2_check_minutes"},"co2_step_ppm":{
"doc":"\nHow far CO2 must move from the last report to send a new one at a check. Also the hysteresis of\nthe CO2 limit.\n\n","uiName":"CO2 Step","unit":"ppm","default":50,"min":0,"max":5000,"size":4,"translate":1,"id":187,"type":"input","name":"co2_step_ppm"},"dark_poll_minutes":{
"doc":"\nMinutes between CO2 samples while the room is dark.\n\n","uiName":"Dark Sample Interval","unit":"Minutes","default":5,"min":1,"max":60,"size":1,"translate":1,"id":168,"type":"input","name":"dark_poll_minutes"},"lit_poll_minutes":{
"doc":"\nMinutes between CO2 samples while the lights are on.\n\n","uiName":"Lit Sample Interval","unit":"Minutes","default":2,"min":1,"max":60,"size":1,"translate":1,"id":169,"type":"input","name":"lit_poll_minutes"},"high_poll_minutes":{
"doc":"\nMinutes between CO2 samples while CO2 is above the limit, whatever the light.\n\n","uiName":"High CO2 Sample Interval","unit":"Minutes","default":1,"min":1,"max":60,"size":1,"translate":1,"id":170,"type":"input","name":"high_poll_minutes"},"lit_lux":{
"doc":"\nThe light level, read every minute, from which the room counts as lit. It counts as dark again\nbelow half of it.\n\n","uiName":"Lights On Level","unit":"Lux","default":20,"min":0,"max":65535,"size":4,"translate":1,"id":188,"type":"input","name":"lit_lux"},"air_report_values":{
"doc":"\nWhich values the report carries besides the CO2 values and co2_state, added together:\n1 air_temperature, 2 air_humidity and 4 air_pressure. The default 3 sends temperature and\nhumidity.\n\n","uiName":"Air Report Values","unit":"Bit field","default":3,"min":0,"max":7,"size":1,"translate":1,"id":171,"type":"input","name":"air_report_values"},"GPS_TIME_MAX_AGE":{
"doc":"Once this maximum age has passed the device will no longer trust its GPS_TIME and GNSS scans become autonomous.\nAlso, it will start emitting DEVICE_TIME requests on the LoRaWan network once 80% of this time has passed.\nTypically the clock drift is a few seconds per 24 hrs. Gps time should be correct within 30s for good assisted scans.\nOutdoor use tends to increase clock drift.\n\n","uiName":"Device Time Max Age","readOnly":false,"unit":"Seconds","default":0,"min":0,"max":4294967295,"translate":1,"id":205,"type":"register","name":"GPS_TIME_MAX_AGE"},"SATELLITE_COUNT":{
"doc":"\nReads as the number of satellites seen in the last GNSS scan.\n\n","readOnly":true,"unit":"integer","translate":1,"id":206,"type":"register","name":"SATELLITE_COUNT"},"LINKCHECK_TIME":{
"doc":"How long the device goes without hearing anything from the network before it gives the network up and\ngoes to unjoined. Any downlink starts the time again, an acknowledgement as much as a message.\n\nIt asks for an answer well before then. From half of this time on, every uplink it sends is confirmed.\nFrom 80% on it also sends a confirmed link check of its own, even with nothing else to send, and\nrepeats it until something comes back. Those uplinks count towards LORA_RESEND_COUNT as well, so when\nthe network has really gone away the device usually unjoins through that count before this time is up.\n\n0 turns the check off, and then reads back as 0xFFFFFFFF. Any other value outside 300-2592000 is ignored\nand the previous one kept. The firmware sets it back to 86400 on every boot, so an application that\nwants another value writes it in a once rule.\n\nIn the unjoined state the application's own rejoin method is used; the firmware does not rejoin by itself.\n\n","uiName":"Downlink Timeout","readOnly":false,"unit":"Seconds","min":300,"max":2592000,"default":345600,"translate":1,"id":208,"type":"register","name":"LINKCHECK_TIME","used":true},"TX_POWER_RANGE":{
"doc":"Set the power index range for fast ADR, LSB = lowest, MSB = highest\nRange for each is 16 (DR0/Max power) - 0 (regions best), mixing up\nhighest and lowest does not matter (firmware always use the highest of the two as the max).\nThere is a high impact on power consumption to turn this up (lower battery time).\n\n\n","uiName":"TX Power Range","readOnly":false,"min":0,"max":65535,"unit":"2 bytes","translate":1,"id":216,"type":"register","name":"TX_POWER_RANGE","used":true}}